                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3342b240-13c0-36cd-afc6-536e786c1b78",
                        "entry_id": "82a66df5-8a16-3356-b817-7b253a3c5a7b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "филос. методологический подход в философии, заключающийся в абсолютизации относительности и условности знаний и отрицании на этом основании возможности познания объективной истины"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e43ca89-807a-4a45-a9ab-0a9663d07ef0",
                                "sense_id": "3342b240-13c0-36cd-afc6-536e786c1b78",
                                "text": "Такой релятивизм — не самая прочная база для построения этики."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b76566a-20ca-4335-8440-a0203b7bf9ae",
                                "sense_id": "3342b240-13c0-36cd-afc6-536e786c1b78",
                                "text": "Никакой релятивизм в догматах, определенных Римским Престолом, не был допустим"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "390dbdc2-d4f2-38b5-b621-74c49a96eaef",
                        "entry_id": "82a66df5-8a16-3356-b817-7b253a3c5a7b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. приверженность общей теории относительности Альберта Эйнштейна"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a1a941cd-98f9-43a5-9c15-904725c410a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "82a66df5-8a16-3356-b817-7b253a3c5a7b",
                        "target_lang_word": "relativism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "relativism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a22f497-dd0a-3c45-8932-b33db9c61cb0",
                                        "entry_id": "2dcf490a-6fec-3e34-80f3-642b9982573e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory, especially in ethics or aesthetics, that conceptions of truth and moral values are not absolute but are relative to the persons or groups holding them."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "588c9232-ad18-34a7-81ea-4198943ded01",
                                        "entry_id": "2dcf490a-6fec-3e34-80f3-642b9982573e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A specific such theory, advocated by a particular philosopher or school of thought."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c75b8de0-f9aa-4d26-bfb8-d75d1ff5cb4a",
                                                "sense_id": "588c9232-ad18-34a7-81ea-4198943ded01",
                                                "text": "Following Gilbert Harman’s lead, my own formulation of relativism about the normative domain was based on the classic examples of thoroughgoing relativisms drawn from physics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b8d310fc-413e-4382-bb73-3f626743d57b",
                        "source_entry_id": "82a66df5-8a16-3356-b817-7b253a3c5a7b",
                        "target_lang_word": "relativismo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "relativismo",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06405c02-9c0e-3ae8-bf6e-b737a593fce3",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb77e5b-b3f9-39f3-8fba-b295018687d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Idea o teoría sobre que algunos aspectos de la experiencia, como la moral o la verdad, son relativos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46b3e9e7-cb62-4a2f-a6c5-ebf31deea8d3",
                                                "sense_id": "06405c02-9c0e-3ae8-bf6e-b737a593fce3",
                                                "text": "Por otro lado, la hermenéutica radical de autores como el propio Gadamer y Rorty, supondría una renuncia a la pretensión de objetividad y a todo conocimiento explicativo, con la consecuencia del relativismo"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c74dd7ae-9a6c-336c-ba03-b9f97db80c6d",
                                        "entry_id": "dcb77e5b-b3f9-39f3-8fba-b295018687d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relativismo₁ normativo o formal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87794380-6491-44a6-b6be-ebada7eb607e",
                                                "sense_id": "c74dd7ae-9a6c-336c-ba03-b9f97db80c6d",
                                                "text": "Y la afirmación que todas las normas diferentes procedentes de entornos culturales diferentes tienen igual validez (relativismo normativo)(citando a la teoría ética de Brandt)"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
